ART DIRECTOR'S CHOICE
{{9.pj}}

Check the winner against five lenses:
1. BLIND READING: someone who sees only the picture and the line, without the article: what would they say happened? It must match the message.
2. STAKEHOLDERS: would the communications team of any named company, regulator, government, patient group or professional body reasonably say it mocks, blames, threatens or misrepresents them, or takes a side in an open dispute? Patient queues, elderly figures, scissors, flames, locks, walls or revolving doors next to a named actor are red flags.
3. FACTS AND ENTITIES: any label sits on the object that truly represents that entity; nothing implies facts, outcomes or motives not in the excerpt.
4. LANGUAGE: the line is clear to an executive whose first language is Spanish or Portuguese, uses no title words, nothing sarcastic or hinting at a threat.
5. CRAFT: one clear image, no text beyond the single label, no fake documents or screens, not a cliché.
If the winner passes, keep it. If a minimal change fixes it (drop the label, change one word of the line, remove the people), apply only that. If it cannot be fixed minimally, VETO it and run the same check on the runner-up.

OUTPUT valid JSON only, no fence, no double quotes inside any value:
{"blind_reading":"","decision":"PASS|FIX|VETO","changes":"","final":{"id":"","image":"","visible_details":"","label":"","cover_line":""}}

