STEP 3. REJECT only if: there are real words other than the allowed label of at most two words; the picture plus line would mislead a reader about the gist or could be read as the opposite; the main object is not recognisable; documents or screens full of fake text; clutter with competing ideas; the main subject overlaps the upper-left text area or is cut by the frame; an identifiable face or photorealistic person; suits, ties or briefcases; queues of patients or elderly figures in a story about prices, contracts or rules; anything a named company, regulator, government or patient group could reasonably read as mocking, blaming or threatening them, or taking a side; loud or neon colours. Otherwise APPROVE: a good cover leaves room for the headline to do its job.
